    - id: becker1960
      title: An Economic Analysis of Fertility
      authors: Gary S. Becker
      year: 1960
      finding: Treats children as a durable good whose demand depends on income and on their price; falling fertility with income is not evidence that children are inferior.
    - id: becker1981
      title: A Treatise on the Family
      authors: Gary S. Becker
      year: 1981
      finding: The household as a small factory producing commodities from goods and time; specialisation by comparative advantage gives gains from marriage.

