      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:16hotoz'
    '|a||Draw one family, illustrative numbers in thousands of dollars over a lifetime: children across, everything else up.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:yqnbl3'
    '|b||Say they have four million, counting what she could earn. Each child costs four hundred thousand: half money, half her lost pay.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8360
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1d2w1n3'
    '|a||Their best mix touches the highest indifference curve they can reach: three children.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1ltiawt'
    '|b||Now women''s pay doubles. They''re richer. Shouldn''t they have more children?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5000
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1ey4j9l'
    '|a||Richer, yes: five million. But each child now costs six hundred thousand, because every hour at home costs her twice as much.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1e277o0'
    '|a||The line swings: more of everything else, and fewer children. Two and a half.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:mqvspf'
    '|b||So the substitution effect beats the income effect. Children got dearer faster than the family got richer.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6760
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1vfw9p4'
    '|b||There''s a second twist: quality. Parents also choose how much to put into each child: schooling, lessons, time.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7560
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||Becker and Gregg Lewis showed in 1973 that the two feed each other. The more you put into each child, the dearer one more child becomes.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1smk3ai'
    '|b||Does it hold? In Norway, Black, Devereux and Salvanes found that once birth order is counted, family size barely changes how much schooling children get.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9120
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1he6xl7'
    '|a||So the price of a woman''s time fits the fall in fertility well. The trade between how many and how much is still contested.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:j7il6u'
    '|b||The interaction is one line of algebra. Show the math, or skip it?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5240
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:z4lpzl'
    '|a||Spending is the number of children times quality times price. Add one child, and you add quality times price: dearer when each child gets more.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11400
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Add a bit of quality, and you pay it for every child: n times price.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4960
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1kt6mfa'
    '|a||So when one rises, the other gets dearer. That''s why the two tend to move in opposite directions.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1wx1cbv'
    '|a||So one model explains a marriage and a family size.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4480
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||But whose choice is it?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2400
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1kc7ez7'
    '|a||Becker''s household has one set of tastes and one budget: a unitary family. Who brings the money home makes no difference.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1m4or8y'
    '|b||From 1980, economists such as Marilyn Manser and Murray Brown, and later Pierre-André Chiappori, drew two people instead, who bargain, each with something to lose.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11360
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:bdkhnj'
    '|a||Then who holds the money matters. In the late 1970s Britain gave a natural experiment:':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:d92jok'
    '|a||a big child allowance moved from a tax break, mostly in fathers'' pay, to cash paid to mothers.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1hnpf3n'
    '|b||Shelly Lundberg, Robert Pollak and Terence Wales looked at what families bought. Spending on women''s and children''s clothing rose, relative to men''s.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8640
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:rq9out'
    '|a||From wallet to purse, and the spending moved. One family, one budget, doesn''t survive that.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:2e5ut1'
    '|b||Feminist economists went further. Barbara Bergmann called some of Becker''s conclusions preposterous: the family as harmony, and the wage gap that drives specialising taken as given.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12200
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:xmxrt6'
    '|a||And norms, not prices, show up in the data. In American couples, the share of wives who earn a bit more than their husbands drops sharply just past half.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:jkh737'
    '|a||How sure are we? That money is not simply pooled: mostly agreed. That the price of time helped cut fertility: mostly agreed.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:7fxn5s'
    '|b||But across rich countries since the late eighties, where more women work there are more children, not fewer. Why is contested.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7880
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1wfg48y'
    '|b||Three cases to try the ideas on. A microcredit programme lends to wives instead of husbands; the household''s total income is the same either way. What does the unitary model predict for what the household buys?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 14000
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:vn48qh'
    '|b||Nothing changes: with one budget only the total counts. The bargaining evidence says otherwise.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6120
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||Men''s wages rise; women''s stay put. In Becker''s model, what happens to the number of children?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6960
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||More children: the family is richer, and a child''s price, mostly her time, has not changed.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6320
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Two partners earn the same and are equally good at home. Comparative advantage gives them nothing, yet Becker still predicts they specialise. Why?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8760
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|b||Practice makes each better at their half: skills grow with use, so even identical partners gain by specialising over time.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7480
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||So can economics explain marriage and children? It explains a surprising amount: who specialises, and why richer families have fewer children.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9800
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||But a family is two people bargaining inside norms, not one firm with one purse.':
